    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>Eigen has both sparse LU and sparse QR.</div><div><br></div><div>Here an example with LU:</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:none 0% 0% repeat scroll rgb(248,248,248)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,153);font-weight:bold\">#<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">include</span> &lt;TMB.hpp&gt;</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">template</span>&lt;<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">class</span> Type&gt;\r\nType objective_function&lt;Type&gt;::<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">operator</span>() ()\r\n{\r\n  DATA_SPARSE_MATRIX(M);\r\n  PARAMETER_VECTOR(y);\r\n  Eigen::SparseLU&lt; Eigen::SparseMatrix&lt;Type&gt;, Eigen::COLAMDOrdering&lt;<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">int</span>&gt; &gt; lu;\r\n  lu.compute(M);\r\n  matrix&lt;Type&gt; x = lu.solve(y.matrix());\r\n  REPORT(x);\r\n  <span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-weight:bold\">return</span> x.<span style=\"color:rgb(0,134,179)\">array</span>().sum();\r\n}\r\n</span></span>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdj5gYGBjcHA8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PiNpbmNsdWRlICZsdDtUTUIuaHBwJmd0Ozxicj50ZW1wbGF0\r\nZSZsdDtjbGFzcyBUeXBlJmd0Ozxicj5UeXBlIG9iamVjdGl2ZV9mdW5jdGlvbiZsdDtUeXBlJmd0\r\nOzo6b3BlcmF0b3IoKSAoKTxicj57PGJyPiZuYnNwOyBEQVRBX1NQQVJTRV9NQVRSSVgoTSk7PGJy\r\nPiZuYnNwOyBQQVJBTUVURVJfVkVDVE9SKHkpOzxicj4mbmJzcDsgRWlnZW46OlNwYXJzZUxVJmx0\r\nOyBFaWdlbjo6U3BhcnNlTWF0cml4Jmx0O1R5cGUmZ3Q7LCBFaWdlbjo6Q09MQU1ET3JkZXJpbmcm\r\nbHQ7aW50Jmd0OyAmZ3Q7IGx1Ozxicj4mbmJzcDsgbHUuY29tcHV0ZShNKTs8YnI+Jm5ic3A7IG1h\r\ndHJpeCZsdDtUeXBlJmd0OyB4ID0gbHUuc29sdmUoeS5tYXRyaXgoKSk7PGJyPiZuYnNwOyBSRVBP\r\nUlQoeCk7PGJyPiZuYnNwOyByZXR1cm4geC5hcnJheSgpLnN1bSgpOzxicj59PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5g\r\nYGA8L2Rpdj4=\" style=\"min-height:0px;width:0px;max-height:0px;max-width:0px;overflow:hidden;font-size:0em;padding:0px;margin:0px\">​</div></div><div></div><div><br></div><div></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);display:block;padding:0.5em;color:rgb(51,51,51);background:none 0% 0% repeat scroll rgb(248,248,248)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">## Data and parameters</span>\r\nset.seed(<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>)\r\nn &lt;- <span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1e4</span>\r\nM &lt;- Matrix::bandSparse(n, k=-<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>:<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>,diag=list(rnorm(n-<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>),rnorm(n),rnorm(n-<span style=\"color:rgb(0,128,128)\">1</span>)))\r\ny &lt;- rnorm(n)\r\ndata &lt;- list(M=M)\r\nparameters &lt;- list(y=y)\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">## Make a function object</span>\r\nobj &lt;- MakeADFun(data, parameters)\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,136);font-style:italic\">## Test</span>\r\nobj$fn(y)\r\nsum(solve(M,y))\r\n</span></span>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdj5gYGByPC9kaXY+PGRpdj4jIyBEYXRhIGFuZCBwYXJhbWV0ZXJzPGJyPnNldC5zZWVkKDEp\r\nPGJyPm4gJmx0Oy0gMWU0PGJyPk0gJmx0Oy0gTWF0cml4OjpiYW5kU3BhcnNlKG4sIGs9LTE6MSxk\r\naWFnPWxpc3Qocm5vcm0obi0xKSxybm9ybShuKSxybm9ybShuLTEpKSk8YnI+eSAmbHQ7LSBybm9y\r\nbShuKTxicj5kYXRhICZsdDstIGxpc3QoTT1NKTxicj5wYXJhbWV0ZXJzICZsdDstIGxpc3QoeT15\r\nKTxicj4jIyBNYWtlIGEgZnVuY3Rpb24gb2JqZWN0PGJyPm9iaiAmbHQ7LSBNYWtlQURGdW4oZGF0\r\nYSwgcGFyYW1ldGVycywgRExMPSJsdSIpPGJyPiMjIFRlc3Q8YnI+b2JqJGZuKHkpPGJyPnN1bShz\r\nb2x2ZShNLHkpKTxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PmBgYDwvZGl2Pg==\" style=\"min-height:0px;width:0px;max-height:0px;max-width:0px;overflow:hidden;font-size:0em;padding:0px;margin:0px\">​</div></div><div></div><div><br></div><div>The approach has the usual downside when taping algorithms, that it might use parameter dependent branching internally. Also, it&#39;s not as fast as an atomic sparse LU would be.</div><div><br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"auto\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thursday, June 29, 2023 at 1:52:22 AM UTC+2 <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">james...@gmail.com</a> wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>Does anyone know an efficient way in TMB to compute <img alt=\"\\mathbf{vM}^{-1}\" title=\"\\mathbf{vM}^{-1}\" src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/7foDbzAzM4Cw6qXqshylXS6H3rnuBp206xmfM4V4dgmWAaYePHlTaffrxGXD4yXCTwTSc_nj3MqSdneZY_OeTSdf8J02vq-h7oy8eHjBUCVbe3ro-DMh1cpq2HDTuzLwv_j9y5T3VJn0Ju5SRJl2oA=s0-d-e1-ft#https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?zoom=3&amp;bg=ffffff&amp;fg=000000&amp;s=0&amp;latex=%5Cmathbf%7BvM%7D%5E%7B-1%7D\" style=\"display:inline\" height=\"14\" width=\"41\"> where <img alt=\"\\mathbf{M}\" title=\"\\mathbf{M}\" src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/SPDugUVK9d09IdhsZ6ynUSyxAlDFYTAVMfsLl3ccGpg696f9Y57BLXYc8TdJQmZ0SZQeswqGaHVi3gpo4MLnrrI2k9x6bnt3TbEF9gocCX8ddJ-LWPzV_r_jKew5t8fXW5zRHQ=s0-d-e1-ft#https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?zoom=3&amp;bg=ffffff&amp;fg=000000&amp;s=0&amp;latex=%5Cmathbf%7BM%7D\" style=\"display:inline\" height=\"11\" width=\"16\"> is a large, square, sparse, asymmetric matrix and <img alt=\"\\mathbf{v}\" title=\"\\mathbf{v}\" src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/e7kF2HVED9GyipUsVXSp4ikEdDidw8n-djxdvdOtbpEpvQXFQrp91YlfsZ7iPQnmH_6Qs3KY_7PoCuRuz6lSj6vk9j32Yf3H7Zv-7RqeS4IAiA2XM2ThWOa3jKJwmd8NoQ3qkw=s0-d-e1-ft#https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?zoom=3&amp;bg=ffffff&amp;fg=000000&amp;s=0&amp;latex=%5Cmathbf%7Bv%7D\" style=\"display:inline\" height=\"7\" width=\"9\"> is a vector (i.e., without forming <img alt=\"\\mathbf{M}^{-1}\" title=\"\\mathbf{M}^{-1}\" src=\"https://ci5.googleusercontent.com/proxy/s18_SWd1rUbb4HwEabQ2UfU32l_YZ41xQGIAODMy3iGRXfLVPYtByOxahq43I102m61aZ8pBZfRGmPAijZy_-3SC9Kpe5x1_8iwPHuLCvz6WL7dQ1vnj51orRJMo53wojNGcQ5Yj0vF0cbev1Wvh=s0-d-e1-ft#https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?zoom=3&amp;bg=ffffff&amp;fg=000000&amp;s=0&amp;latex=%5Cmathbf%7BM%7D%5E%7B-1%7D\" style=\"display:inline\" height=\"13\" width=\"30\"> in memory)?</div><div><br></div><div>It seems like R-package Matrix can do this using a &quot;sparseQR&quot; decomposition (presumably using options that are also in the Eigen package), but I don&#39;t see this functionality <a href=\"https://kaskr.github.io/adcomp/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://kaskr.github.io/adcomp/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792461741642000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3hNRabJSYunHTVig2GzWs_\">documented</a> in TMB.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Jim</div></div>\r\n</blockquote></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
